    "comment": "2026-10-07 concrete proposed origin/account contract, superseding the previously unselected engineering options in the note while preserving historical proposals and comments. docs/notes/2026-10-07-first-represented-life-boundary.md sections 6–8 now select exact integer picogram-C accounting from actual final-parent bulk mass/composition, a versioned bounded habitat allocation/accessibility/origin prescription, one persisted-book lineage scope, retry-safe ordered operations, a sole serial lifecycle settlement and explicit terminal export to an unresolved physical boundary. Normalized ecology biomass never becomes kg C; no new gravitating mass or cross-history identity promise. Tuning values are prescriptions, not measured biology. Standard core/envelope births do not initially meet both positive H and the 225–375K guard: gas-free cores discard H, while positive envelopes beyond the 170K snowline start below 190.4975K under the current seed-temperature law. Later evolution is not ruled out; no complete natural final-parent admission or useful account lifetime has been observed. Retention-species labels cannot supply an elemental inventory. Guards remain unchanged. The note names finite later implementation slices and leaves the meaningful resource-action/rate producer unfinished; this does not complete the whole specification acceptance. Independent intent_research source/accounting/applicability review found no publication blocker at note SHA256 79136b693aa6e6f49f57947dd08e63f2e963ee13215bef47d6a919dd4cc25417; root accepted publication scope only. Same Incoming 3, original body and prior provenance preserved; no source/tests/native work, implementation admission or external review credit. Evidence: .ημ/diagnostics/life-actor-planning/origin-account-contract-audit.json and chemistry-prerequisite-audit.json; closure recorded in origin-contract-closure.json.",
